WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.233
Clip 1: In a portrait view, a G1 robot takes steps from the floor onto a padded incline. An overhead safety tether and an operator holding its controller remain visible.

00:04.233 --> 00:06.233
Hard cut to Clip 2, a separate landscape recording. The robot stands beside a padded incline, attached to a gantry. An operator stands to the left.

00:06.233 --> 00:11.233
The robot steps forward and bends its torso, lowering a handheld tool toward the padded surface. The safety tether remains attached above its shoulders.

00:11.233 --> 00:13.233
The robot straightens from the bent posture.

00:13.233 --> 00:16.233
The tether becomes taut and the gantry lifts the robot as it resets toward the starting position.

00:16.233 --> 00:20.233
Hard cut to Clip 3, another laboratory trial. The robot steps forward, then begins lowering its torso over the padded surface.

00:20.233 --> 00:24.233
The robot bends deeply and lowers its hand and tool near the surface, then shifts backward while bending its knees. The operator holds the gantry controller.

00:24.233 --> 00:29.233
The robot settles into a low crouched posture beside the incline, then brings its torso more upright while its knees remain bent.

00:29.233 --> 00:33.034
The robot rises and is lifted by the overhead tether during reset. All three excerpts preserve original speed; the labels identify separate recordings. No sound is included.
